# L §8.5 WARN-UNREAD (tally 2.1.2, issue #30, the user's "A: warn only if never named"): a place no line names warns
# `place <x> is read by nothing`. savings is named by pay's leg and nothing totals it: no warning (a leg naming the place
# is a use). idle is named only by its opening row, a row keyed by the place: it warns. shop is an outside place no leg
# names: it warns too (an outside place has no exception; it exists to be a leg's other end).
=== m.tally
model t
  tally 2
  on 2026-06-30
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31

source s "s"
unit PLN: currency minor 0.01
input wage: money PLN
input day: date
place konto: accounts PLN lives 2026-01-01..
place savings: accounts PLN lives 2026-01-01..
place idle: accounts PLN lives 2026-01-01..
place world: outside lives 1900-01-01..
place shop: outside lives 1900-01-01..

move pay: transfers
  on day
  leg cash from world to savings amount wage

ask q: bal(konto, 2026-03-31)

version v
  cite s
  governs always
  known 2026-01-01
  wage = 100.00 PLN
  day = 2026-02-10
  opening[konto] = 5.00 PLN at 2026-01-01 start
  opening[savings] = 0 PLN at 2026-01-01 start
  opening[idle] = 0 PLN at 2026-01-01 start
=== expect
q: 5.00 PLN
  cut 2026-06-30
warning: WARN-UNREAD place idle is read by nothing
warning: WARN-UNREAD place shop is read by nothing
